    "processing": "Official named areas retained. Danish parishes that cross municipal boundaries keep one identity and the same complete land geometry in each overlapping municipality; the largest overlap is used for primary navigation. Swedish local areas use the original GISCO municipality outline with detailed OpenStreetMap masks for Mälaren, Storsjön, Vänern and Vättern, restoring land removed by the coarse overview lake mask. Other areas are clipped to their existing municipality. Shared local topology simplified by 0.00003 degrees (about 3 m north–south), then clipped to the existing municipality land mask. Existing regional and municipal geometry is unchanged. Uncovered coastal slivers keep the municipality backdrop; no local administrative units or population estimates are invented.",
